          "body": "Queries with joins or cross products could evaluate a throwing filter before its guard (duckdb/duckdb#26098). A query with `b < 1 AND get_bit('1'::BIT, b) = 1` failed on bit index `2` instead of returning no rows, and `sub.s::INT` tried to convert `'x'` despite `s <> 'x'` inside the subquery. Integer division and CSV inputs were also affected. These queries return the correct results in v1.5.6.\n\n`FilterPushdown::PushdownProjection` keeps throwing predicates above a projection. Projection pullup, introduced in v2 by duckdb/duckdb#20967, removed that projection, leaving stacked filters with the guard below. `RelationManager::ExtractJoinRelations` collected them from the top down, so the join order optimizer combined them with the throwing predicate first. Expression reordering preserves that order when filters can throw.\n\nThe change collects each stacked filter chain bottom first, preserving evaluation order and the position of join conditions. Compared default plans, including arithmetic filters over joins, are unchanged; with `filter_pushdown` disabled, stacked predicates now appear bottom first. A join inside the subquery acting as a guard remains outside this change (duckdblabs/bot-issue-tracker#672): keeping the projection would fix it, but would stop filters such as `t.i * 2 > 5` from being pushed below a join because `CanThrow` holds for integer `+` and `*`. Filters pushed into `EXCEPT` and `INTERSECT` inputs are tracked in duckdblabs/bot-issue-tracker#673 and also fail on v1.5.6. The new `test/optimizer/projection_pullup_filter_order.test` covers `get_bit`, casts, integer division, CSV input and three chained guards. Every query fails on `main` and passes in `reldebug` and an assertion build with sanitizers, including prepared statements, statement copy, disabled optimization, statement serialization and plan serialization. All 426 optimizer, join, filter and projection pullup test files pass. The full unit suite passes except tests that also fail on `main`: `reset_threads.test` under the runner’s `--max-threads`, `external_resource_logging.test`, `external_resource_lifecycle.test`, `connect_passthrough_quack.test` in its group, and httpfs’s `http_logging.test`.\n\nFixes duckdblabs/bot-issue-tracker#346\nRelated: duckdb/duckdb#26098\n\nTo clarify, I'm an autonomous bot following workflows described by the DuckDB maintainers. Take what I say and do with a grain of salt. You can find more information, or report concerns about my behavior, in this repository: https://github.com/duckdb-bot/guidelines\n\nagent_version:8ca2944e36c75c348a14af69198598982374be98\n",
